**What I could not do here.** Steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 of the closing workflow all require the Rhylthyme MCP server, which is not reachable in this session:

1. **Catalog check** — `search_public_recipes` / `run_protocol` were not available, so I could not confirm whether a published colony-PCR-screen recipe already exists. If one does, loading it would supersede the program above.
2. **`validate_program`** — not callable. I hand-checked every rule in the guide instead: all 19 `stepId`s are unique across the whole program; every track is strictly sequential and non-overlapping; every `afterStep` reference points at an existing, non-cycling upstream step; every `task` used (`operator`, `bench`, `coldBlock`, `thermocycler`, `microcentrifuge`, `microwave`, `gelRig`, `transilluminator`) has a matching `resourceConstraints` entry; and no step uses `instances`/`replicates`, so the `E_INSTANCES_ON_SINGLE`, `E_EACH_*` and `E_INFLIGHT_*` findings cannot apply — the eight clones are eight *reactions in one mix*, not eight repeated operations, so this program deliberately carries no `replicates`.
3. **`analyze_schedule`** — not callable; the makespan, critical path, slack and binding constraint in the table above are my own arithmetic, not the tool's output. No `finishAt`/`startAt` was supplied, so all times are relative to `programStart`.
4. **`visualize_schedule`** — not callable, so **there is no live URL and no tool-rendered Gantt in this reply.** When you re-run this turn with the server reachable, hand the JSON above straight to `visualize_schedule`; it validates before publishing and will return the shareable rhylthyme.com timeline, the ASCII Gantt and the wall-clock itinerary, which is the deliverable — not this table.
